  "notes": "<div><font size=\"5\"><b>LED lights and groups</b></font></div><div>A stage of LED lights: four RGBW pars at the front, four RGB pars at the back, an LED bar of four cells and a hazer. The stack is made of the lights of the stage and their groups only: no memory, no channel.</div><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">What is in it</font></b></div><ul><li><b>Stage</b>: the plan of the rig. Each light knows its channels (D dims, R G B W mix the color), so the desk plays it as a light, not as loose channels.</li><li>Groups: Front, Back and All washes. A group plays its lights together.</li><li>The stack: each cue lights a light or a group in a color, at a level, over its times. The next cue takes it down again.</li><li>Memory 1: a chase over the back pars, made of light steps with a color each.</li></ul><div><b><font color=\"#ffb020\">Try it</font></b></div><ol><li>Open <b>Fixtures</b>: every light with its fader and its color; the groups under them. Move a fader, choose a color: the light follows, and <b>Stage</b> shows it.</li><li>Press <b>Stack</b> and go through the cues with <b>GO</b>. On the <b>Stack</b> view each cue names its light or group, with its color.</li><li>Make a cue of your own: on the <b>Stack</b> view, <b>Add cue</b>, then choose Group as its kind, and a color.</li><li>On <b>Stage</b>, <b>Edit</b> lets you move the lights, change their channels, and make new ones.</li></ol><div>A light that is missing in a group, or a group that is gone, makes its cues play nothing: the cues say so.</div>",
